==================== KAFKA COMPLETE LEARNING ROADMAP ====================

🟢 LEVEL 1 — BASIC KAFKA
1.  Broker
2.  Cluster
3.  Producer
4.  Consumer
5.  Topic
6.  Message / Record
7.  Key
8.  Partition
9.  Offset
10. Consumer Group
11. Leader / Follower
12. Replication


🟡 LEVEL 2 — PRODUCER SIDE
13. KafkaTemplate
14. ProducerRecord
15. Serializer
16. JSON Serialization
17. Producer Acknowledgement (acks)
18. Retries
19. Idempotent Producer
20. Batching
21. Compression
22. Partitioner


🟠 LEVEL 3 — CONSUMER SIDE
23. @KafkaListener
24. ConsumerRecord
25. Deserializer
26. JSON Deserialization
27. Auto Commit
28. Manual Commit
29. Offset Commit
30. Consumer Poll
31. Consumer Lag
32. Consumer Rebalancing
33. Partition Assignment


🔵 LEVEL 4 — RELIABILITY / ERROR HANDLING
34. Acknowledgement Mode
35. Retry
36. Error Handler
37. Dead Letter Topic (DLT)
38. @RetryableTopic
39. Duplicate Messages
40. Idempotency
41. At-most-once Delivery
42. At-least-once Delivery
43. Exactly-once Delivery


🟣 LEVEL 5 — KAFKA ARCHITECTURE
44. Replication Factor
45. ISR (In-Sync Replicas)
46. Controller
47. Broker Failure
48. Partition Leader Election
49. Data Retention
50. Log Segment
51. Log Compaction
52. __consumer_offsets


🔴 LEVEL 6 — ADVANCED KAFKA
53. Transactions
54. Exactly Once Semantics (EOS)
55. Kafka Streams
56. KStream
57. KTable
58. State Store
59. Kafka Connect
60. Source Connector
61. Sink Connector
62. Schema Registry
63. Avro
64. Protobuf


🚀 LEVEL 7 — PRODUCTION / REAL WORLD
65. Kafka Security
66. SSL / TLS
67. SASL
68. ACL
69. Authentication vs Authorization
70. Monitoring
71. Consumer Lag Monitoring
72. Throughput
73. Performance Tuning
74. Partition Planning
75. Replication Planning





